Z||000000||85Josh||08-08-2001||09:00 PM||||I just pulled the clutch out of my 85 2M4 5-speed. The friction ring of the disk had actually ripped loose from the center, spring-loaded section! The flywheel and pressure plate both look like new. The clutch is a Sachs brand, is that OE? I'm replacing it with a Cumberland from AutoZone, anyone have a similar experience with this brand? TIA<P>------------------<BR>85 2M4(Lil' Bit)||||reg||5
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||08-08-2001||11:36 PM||||Stock clutch is Borg Warner.<BR>I get them new.<P>Is the Cumberland new or a re-man unit?||||reg||1
Z||000002||85Josh||08-09-2001||05:12 AM||||Indy, they told me it is new. On closer examiniation, the Sachs had 4 springs, and the Cumberland has 6, slightly smaller springs. Other details appear to be better built as well, although the sheetmetal pieces that hold the friction surface to the center disk seems to be the same thickness.||||reg||1
